## Recheck Focus
1. Issues from the previous report should be retained in results if the current modifications do not clearly fix them.
2. Only remove an old issue when the post-repair segment has clearly fixed it, or the issue existed only in the replaced old segment.
3. Check whether the post-repair segments introduce new prompt leaks, intra-chapter factual contradictions, identity/name errors, or obvious expression errors; cross-chapter boundaries and causal chains are handled by other modules.
4. If an old issue cannot be confirmed as fixed using only local segments, conservatively continue retaining it.
